WEBVTT

00:02:28.916 --> 00:02:34.149
I had known him when
I was a graduate student at Berkeley.

00:02:34.173 --> 00:02:36.044
And I had some ideas,

00:02:36.068 --> 00:02:38.515
and I brought them to him
and he liked them.

00:02:38.539 --> 00:02:45.165
Together, we did this work
which you can easily see up there.

00:02:45.189 --> 00:02:46.339
There it is.

00:02:47.198 --> 00:02:50.804
CA: It led to you publishing
a famous paper together.

00:02:50.828 --> 00:02:54.066
Can you explain at all what that work was?

00:02:55.028 --> 00:02:56.186
JS: No.

00:02:56.210 --> 00:02:58.484
(Laughter)

00:02:58.966 --> 00:03:01.030
JS: I mean, I could
explain it to somebody.